===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pleh₁-}}
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:compleet<t:full,complete>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|compleet|t=full, complete}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|complet}} or {{der|en|la|completus}}, past participle of {{m|la|compleō|t=to fill up, to complete}} (whence also {{m|en|complement}}, {{m|en|compliment}}), from {{m|la|com-}} + {{m|la|pleō|t=to fill, to fulfill}} (whence also {{m|en|deplete}}, {{m|en|replete}}, {{m|en|plenty}}), ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*pleh₁-|t=to fill}} ({{cog|en|full}}).

